 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 459851,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You are taking a multiple-choice test with 10 questions where each question has 5 possible answers: (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e). You did not study, so you will guess at each question. What is the probability of getting exactly 5 questions correct?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.026"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "To determine the value of p, consider the probability of obtaining a correct answer by guessing there will be 1 correct answer out of the 5 possible multiple-choice answers.<br>\nApply the binomial probability formula where <span data-math=\"n = 10,\\;p = \\frac{1}{5} = 0.20,\\mathrm{and}\\;x = 5\"></span><br>\n\nSubstituting these values into the binomial probability formula, the probability for 5 successes can be calculated as follows:<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\begin{array}{*{20}{c}}\n{P\\left( x \\right)}&amp; = &amp;{\\frac{{n!}}{{\\left( {n - x} \\right)!x!\\;}}{p^x}\\;{{\\left( {1 - p} \\right)}^{n - x}}}\\\\\n{P\\left( 5 \\right)}&amp; = &amp;{\\frac{{10!}}{{\\left( {10 - 5} \\right)!5!\\;}}{{0.20}^5}\\;{{\\left( {1 - 0.20} \\right)}^{10 - 5}}}\\\\\n{P\\left( 5 \\right)}&amp; = &amp;{\\frac{{10!}}{{5!5!\\;}}{{0.20}^5}\\;{{\\left( {0.80} \\right)}^5}}\\\\\n{P\\left( 5 \\right)}&amp; = &amp;{252\\left({0.00032} \\right)\\;\\left( {0.32768} \\right)}\\\\\n{P\\left( 5 \\right)}&amp; = &amp;{0.026}\n\\end{array}\"></span><br>\nThe same probability answer can be obtained using technology, as follows:<br><br>\nExcel: In any empty cell, type in the command: <br>\n=BINOM.DIST(5,10,0.2,FALSE)<br><br>\nPython:<br> \nType in the commands:<br>\n<pre class=\"python\" lang=\"python\"># import statistics library \nfrom scipy.stats import binom\nbinom.pmf(5, 10, 0.2)<br>\nThe resulting output will look like this:\n0.026 </pre>\n"
    }
   ],
